{"id": "EUVD-2026-96576", "enisaUuid": "d4fc2431-79d6-37b0-80d5-f1f33efaca4c", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows low-privileged authenticated users to remove user group members by calling DELETE /sys/user/deleteUserGroupBatch. Attackers can supply any groupId and comma-separated userIds to delete sys_ugroup_user rows without permission or tenant checks, tampering with administrator-maintained groups.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:03:17", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_user_group_member_removal_batch.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysUserController.java#L851-L866", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-deleteusergroupbatch-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-26w9-3rx3-xg95", "CVE-2026-108637"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d2ef709a-4c5d-36a1-b889-adde3acbc838", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7d0e31f9-f8db-37f5-b1be-15226b0953f8", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}